{
  "_comment": "Every product needs a PricebookEntry to be quotable, each carrying ProductSellingModelId (README landmine). Metered products are 0.00 here — their price is the rate card entry. The commitment is 1.00 per unit so the quote quantity IS the committed amount; the CSM fee is 0.00 and priced on the line. TWO ENTRIES PER PRODUCT, USD AND EUR: the pricing decision table and the quote's product search only serve rows in the corporate currency (USD) — 14 EUR-only rows were invisible all day on 2026-10-07 — while a quote line saves only against an entry in the quote's currency (EUR here). Same prices in both; 0.00 and 1.00 are currency-neutral, and the real EUR prices live on the rate card.",
